    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Triumph TF-E Bikes Get Even More Enduro With Updates for the 2027 Model Year\nCitroen Augments Its New C5 and e-C5 Aircross SUV Ranges With Fresh Emerald Trim Level in the UK\n6 photos\nPhoto: Citroen\nOrder books have already opened for the new flagship trim level for the United Kingdom market for the Citroen New C5 and e-C5 Aircross crossover SUVs, with pricing starting from £37,290 MRRP, which is about $50k at the current exchange rate. Ouch, right?\nIf you have been wondering what Citroen has been up to across the UK market as of late, the answer is simple: not much. Instead, they have simply relied on the global news: Sandeep Bhambra’s appointment as Head of Design for Citroen and DS Automobiles, the 2CV Concept along with the sibling Furgonnette prototype striking a chord with the audience at the 2026 Paris Motor Show, or the company’s introduction of the fresh Outdoor trim level for the C3, e-C3, C3 Aircross and its fully electric version.\nWell, now it’s time for a change, and Citroen UK has announced the expansion of the New C5 Aircross lineup with the introduction of the Emerald grade, now the flagship trim level for the hybrid and electric variants. Emerald trim becomes the highest specification option for both, exceeding the previous Max configuration that it builds upon with Drive Assist Pack 2.0, Head-Up Display, and heated front seats and steering wheel, among others.\nThe new trim also marks the introduction of a new premium Emerald Blue metallic paint option, priced at £645 incl. VAT. The Emerald version adds a black roof and Emerald-coloured clips on the front bumper and doors. In the cabin there’s a panoramic opening sunroof, a frameless electrochrome rear-view mirror, grey leather-effect and cloth Advanced Comfort seats, plus Emerald interior detailing and lighting.\nThe company also offers a suspension with Progressive Hydraulic Cushions, as well as a wide array of powertrain options. For example, the Citroen e-C5 Aircross Emerald comes with the 210hp Comfort Range and up to 321 miles (WLTP combined) of range, starting from £38,845 ($52k) with the Electric Car Grant, while the 230hp Long Range version offers up to 421 miles (WLTP combined) of range from £44,965 or $60k.\nCitroen says it maintains a level of affordability, but who are they kidding? These are premium prices; there’s no doubt about it. At least the C5 Aircross Emerald also comes with a meager Hybrid 145 powertrain from £37,290 or a plug-in hybrid version with 195 ponies from £39,860 or $53k. Additionally, the Hybrid Plus, Max, and Emerald variants have a new 19-inch moondust diamond-cut silver and black alloy wheel model.\n“We are excited about the addition of the Emerald trim level, both for its vibrant new shade which perfectly complements the lines of the C5 Aircross, and for its generous level of equipment, including a panoramic sunroof. This trim level marks a continued development of our product range, bringing a more premium specification at an affordable price point,” said Greg Taylor, Managing Director, Citroen UK.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nCitroen C5 and e-C5 Aircross Emerald Citroen C5 Aircross e-C5 Aircross Hybrid EV pricing UK\nRead Press Release\nAbout the author: Aurel Niculescu\nAurel has aimed high all his life (literally, at 16 he was flying gliders all by himself) so in 2006 he switched careers and got hired as a writer at his favorite magazine. Since then, his work has been published both by print and online outlets, most recently right here, on autoevolution. Full profile\nUP NEXT Dealer Selling Restored 1957 Bel Air That Hides Just Two Reasons To Make Buyers Walk Away",
